sum(y - p) / (sum p(1-p) + lambda), lambda 8 for team play-calling, 11 for a receiver, 25 for a quarterback or defense, 6 for a kicker. Yard distributions are mixtures: a player's own plays with weight n / (n + 25 to 40), the league list otherwise.","Play-calling: dropback share by down, distance bucket and score/time context (normal, hurry, milk) from all 2026 plays, plus a shrunk team offset. Fourth-down go / field goal / punt odds come from the league's 2026 fourth downs by field zone and distance, with a late-trailing override (go unless a field goal is within range and within one score).","Dropbacks: sack rate (offence x defence), scramble rate (QB), interception rate (QB x defence), then a target drawn by the team's 2026 target share. Completion odds = league + QB + receiver + defence offsets. Yards come from the receiver's own completions or the league list scaled by team and opponent yards-per-completion. Runs: a rusher drawn by carry share, yards from his own carries or the league list, scaled by the opponent's yards per carry allowed. Touchdowns happen when the yards reach the goal line, so there is no separate touchdown rate to invent.","Other pieces: accepted penalties (rate x opponent rate, yards and automatic-first-down share from the file), fumbles lost, interception and fumble return yards, safeties, punts (the punter's gross and return distribution), field goals (a logistic curve in kick distance fit on 2026 kicks, plus a shrunk kicker offset), extra points and two-point tries at the 2026 league rates, kickoff starting spots from 2026 drives that began on a kickoff.","Clock: seconds to the next snap are drawn from 2026 plays of the same type and context, so hurry-up and clock-killing tempo come from the file. Teams kneel to end the game. Timeouts, the two-minute warning, onside kicks, challenges, injuries, weather and home-field advantage are not modelled.","Overtime: ten minutes, a random coin toss, both teams get a possession unless the defence scores; after that, sudden death. Still tied at the end: a tie.","10,000 games are simulated with seeds 2026.. (one seed per game, so the whole run reproduces). The most typical game is the simulated game with the smallest standardised distance to the medians of: both teams' points (counted twice), the margin, both teams' total yards, both teams' turnovers and the total number of plays."],"model":{"fg_curve":{"intercept_at_40":2.4493030689068034,"per_yard":-0.1146165648658033,"n_kicks":390},"xp":0.9417249417249417,"two_point":0.5581395348837209,"league":{"comp":0.6562243726422831,"sack":0.06118955926401369,"interception":0.020876826722338204,"yards_per_comp":10.941514621344664,"yards_per_rush":4.034537246049662}}}